{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared request-signal vectors (docs/SERVER_SDK_SPEC.md, Capability 2b, #236).",
    "Generated by `go test ./internal/reqsignal -update` from internal/reqsignal/vectors_test.go;",
    "the classify, methods, routes and spikes expectations are hand-written there, build is computed.",
    "",
    "`classify`: one finished request to the signal it produces (\"\" = none).",
    "`methods` / `routes`: normalisation before fingerprinting.",
    "`build`: request to count kind, fingerprint signal, expected_fp, template text, raw exemplar.",
    "  Every SDK computes expected_fp with its own fingerprint code (fingerprint_vectors.json).",
    "`invalid_build`: a signal/status pair a sensor must refuse (the sidecar drops it).",
    "`spikes`: steps run in order against one fresh detector. `observe` records `repeat`",
    "  (default 1) identical requests; `tick_ms` is a flush at that time; `end` is process exit.",
    "  `want` is the spikes that step returns, sorted by method then route.",
    "",
    "Changing an expectation changes what customers' apps report: lockstep across every SDK."
  ],
  "constants": {
    "slow_threshold_ms": 3000,
    "spike_window_seconds": 60,
    "spike_min_count": 10,
    "spike_min_percent": 10,
    "max_routes_per_window": 512,
    "max_route_chars": 255,
    "unknown_route": "*",
    "other_method": "OTHER"
  },
  "classify": [
